    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1e5bff11-ae4c-4b3c-a51f-a1212f1c4119&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201580439774_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant and Coordinator of Events",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\n\nLocation: Olivet\n\nThe University of Olivet, a liberal arts institution with a historical commitment to inclusion and social justice, invites applications for the position of Executive Assistant and Coordinator of Events .  The University of Olivet was founded in 1844 as an institution of higher education open to all regardless of race, gender, or ability to pay. The University’s faculty and staff continue its tradition of creating and sustaining a welcoming and inclusive educational environment for students and maintaining its commitment to social justice.  The University is one of the most diverse private liberal arts institutions in the state of Michigan and actively seeks inclusion in its students, faculty, and staff. The undergraduate student body is a mix of urban and rural students from a range of socioeconomic backgrounds, many of whom are first-generation university attendees. The University’s faculty and staff are committed to providing personalized, individualized attention for students who commit themselves to seeking academic and personal success.  The Executive Assistant and Coordinator of Events will dedicate 50% of effort to providing administrative support to the Vice President of Recruitment Marketing and Enrollment in the broad-based functions of the enrollment services division. The remainder of effort is dedicated to the planning, organization, and execution of The University of Olivet events sponsored or executed by the Enrollment Division.  DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Executive Assistant (50%) serves as the primary liaison between on-campus and off-campus constituents on behalf of the Vice President of Recruitment Marketing and Enrollment. This role also provides administrative support for the departments of Admissions and Financial Aid. Duties include:  calendaring, scheduling, facilitating meetings, agendas, and events budget management spending and purchasing inventory management communication and reporting document generation and preservation supervision and management of student workers. reviewing and approving time sheets for payroll  Coordinator of Events (50%) supports the university and Division of Enrollment in the planning, organization and execution of all campus division supported or executed events.  Duties include: event ideation and planning identifying collaborators, including campus and community constituents, as well as experiential opportunities facilitating event planning, production, and execution supply identification and acquisition facilities procurement  budgeting, pricing, and procurement  arranging, managing, and organization of professional and student staffing  transportation, logistics, and execution of events    MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS  Bachelor’s degree. High level of computer literacy Exceptional organizational and communication skills Discretion and diplomacy are required Ability to manage, supervise, and direct colleagues  Decision and delegation abilities are critical DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS  Knowledge of student information systems  Event management experience Supervisory experience  Knowledge of customer relationship management systems High level of proficiency in Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Adobe PHYSICAL AND MENTAL DEMAND -Adequate physical fitness to maintain long hours and busy schedule -Use of gross motor skills to perform supervisory and organizational duties -Use of fine motor skills in operation of keyboard equipment -Problem-solving ability -Ability to understand and work with numbers and data -Ability to see, hear, and speak with or without the use of aids to perform normal office tasks  -Mental capacity to assist with numerous administrative responsibilities   The above statement reflects the general duties considered necessary to describe the principle functions of the job identified, and shall not be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job. It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1e5bff11-ae4c-4b3c-a51f-a1212f1c4119&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201583909554_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "ITS Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Olivet\n\nThe ITS Systems Technician is responsible for the maintenance and repair of IT systems endpoints at The University of Olivet. This includes desktops, laptops, mobile devices, IoTs, multifunction printers, cameras, AV systems, IP phones, and other technologies. The technician ensures optimal performance of voice/data wiring and manages the campus’s audio-visual infrastructure. Collaboration with university departments is key to meeting tech-related expectations, along with evaluating and recommending new IT/AV solutions RESPONSIBILITIES AND ACCOUNTABILITIES 1. Support and maintain the voice and data network infrastructure. 2. Maintain the operation of several campus multi-user computers, and networks, as well as stand-alone networked PCs. 3. Troubleshoot and resolve hardware, software, and network issues. Troubleshoot hardware and software problems and arrange for service if necessary. Coordinate with vendors and manage support ticket resolution workflows. 4. Assist campus departments with administrative process redesign, taking advantage of new technology. 5. Provide second-tier technical support, including responding to and resolving IT support tickets. 6. Support and maintain audio-visual systems across campus. 7. Operate and maintain a diverse collection of computer hardware and software. 8. Maintain the Operation of Systems at student computer labs. 9. Oversee IT equipment inventory and asset tracking. 10. Engage in ongoing professional development and technical training. Perform duties in a diverse and challenging environment. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS - Required: Two years of experience in the PC Support field with extensive knowledge of Microsoft Windows networking or two years of experience in a higher ED institute in computer services or academic/administrative computing field. Must display proficiency with PC software including, Windows OSs and Mac OSs , Microsoft Productivity tools like Office Suite, and knowledge of Windows server platform or MS 365 Cloud (Active Directory and Exchange). Must also have experience troubleshooting PC hardware and peripherals as well as a basic familiarity with computer networks, and cabling. Must be able to troubleshoot voice and network issues. Must be able to operate, troubleshoot, set up, and teardown AV equipment. Preferred: Bachelor’s Degree and three or more years of experience in a higher education institution in the computer services field. Familiarity with IT ticketing system. Customer service experience. Extensive knowledge of Ethernet networks. Experience or knowledge equivalent to MCSE track certification or Cisco track certification. Extensive knowledge and experience in configuring, repairing, and installing PCs Oss, and applications using Microsoft Configuration Manager. Experience with Active Directory user management and familiarity with network password reset, MFA setup, and network account login process. Working Conditions: Standard office setting (on-site); may include exposure to loud environments. Physical activity may include walking across campus and sitting for extended periods",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1e5bff11-ae4c-4b3c-a51f-a1212f1c4119&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201583846103_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Head Men's Volleyball Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Olivet\n\nThe University of Olivet is located in south central Michigan in the town of Olivet, MI, which is a close knit, rural community offering quiet streets and natural surroundings, yet is not more than 30 minutes from the larger cities of Lansing and Battle Creek. Both are small enough to be friendly and large enough to boast many of the big city amenities. The University of Olivet was founded in 1844 on the principle that the future of humanity rests in the hands, hearts and minds of those who will take responsibility for themselves and others in an increasingly diverse society. Open since its founding to all regardless of race, gender or ability to pay, Olivet is one of the most diverse private liberal arts institutions in the state and actively seeks inclusion in its students and employees. The student body is composed of a strong mixture of first-generation, urban, rural and students from all socioeconomic backgrounds, with 50 percent qualifying annually for Federal Pell Grants. The University of Olivet faculty and staff are committed to providing personalized, individualized attention for students who seek academic and personal success. The University of Olivet competes in Division III of the Michigan Intercollegiate Athletic Association, the oldest athletic conference in the nation. Position Summary   The successful candidate will possess the ability to recruit, develop, coach and manage a collegiate men’s volleyball program within the standards of The University of Olivet, the Michigan Intercollegiate Athletic Association (MIAA) and the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA).  Qualifications  The ideal candidate must possess a bachelor’s degree and adequate knowledge about the fundamentals and techniques of volleyball obtained through previously coaching at the high school and/or college level. Must be able to be cleared to drive college vehicles. Along with the educational and sport experience, serious consideration will be given to the candidate who’s characteristics coincide with the following principals: maintain and promote the academic pursuits of The University of Olivet student-athletes; comply with and reinforce the Comet Athletic Program’s rules and mission; acts professionally and communicates appropriately with the College’s students, coaches, administration, staff, alumni and spectators; willingness to develop professionally.  Compensation  Competitive annual salary and comprehensive benefits package, including tuition remission programs.  Application Process  Click on this link: Career Center , select this position and then click on the “Apply” button. From here, follow the instructions for completing the profile, application and uploading your cover letter, resume, and names and contact information for three references. Responsibilities 1.Directs the operations of the The University of Olivet Men’s Volleyball program within the standards of The University of Olivet, the Midwest Collegiate Volleyball League (MCVL), and the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA) 2.Educates/coaches student-athletes in the sport of volleyball. 3.Recruits prospective student-athletes according to the enrollment goals and admissions standards of The University of Olivet and the eligibility requirements of the MCVL and NCAA. 4.Selects team members. 5.Schedules and coordinates competition schedules, team travel accommodations, team tryouts, practices, meetings, individual workouts and conditioning sessions. 6.Coordinates the issuance, care, inventory and collection of equipment, uniforms and supplies for men’s volleyball. Submits appropriate equipment inventory forms to the Athletic Director within the requested times. 7.Manages sport’s budget and coordinate team fund raising activities. 8.Purchases and manages team equipment and supplies. 9.Coordinates facility usage for the men’s volleyball program. 10.Submits complete team roster and inventory forms to the Athletic Director. 11.Ensures the proper completion of physical examinations and all forms relating to the examinations and emergency medical authorization before a student participates.1 2.Manages duties and responsibilities of assistant coaches with the approval of the Athletic Director, as needed. 13.Coordinates and leads at least one team community service project during each academic year. 14.Supervises student-athletes at all times including practices, meetings, workouts, travel and other team functions. 15.Attends all athletic department meetings and appropriate college functions (pep rallies, homecoming, Hall of Fame inductions, etc.). 16.Exhibits appropriate conduct with students, coaches, administration, staff, alumni, spectators, officials and opponents at all times. 17.Collects and submits appropriate student-athlete eligibility forms. 18.Provides leadership that promotes positive attitudes and good sportsmanship. 19.Notifies all members of the team of all Comet Athletic Program’s policies, procedures and training rules as they pertain to the team. 20.Maintains current certifications in CPR and First Aid to be held on file in the Office of Athletics. 21.Submits driving record verification for use of institutional vehicles. 22.Works within the missions and philosophies of the Comet Athletic Program and The University of Olivet. 23.Exhibits personal conduct that promotes attitudes and behaviors among student-athletes that coincide with the policies outlined in the Comet Athletic Handbook. 24.Makes decisions that positively affect the Comet Athletic Program. 25.Maintains a proper perspective regarding the priorities of academics and athletics at The University of Olivet.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1e5bff11-ae4c-4b3c-a51f-a1212f1c4119&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201583842415_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Customer Service Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Olivet\n\nThe University of Olivet was founded in 1844 as an institution of higher education open to all regardless of race, gender, or ability to pay. The University’s faculty and staff continue its tradition of creating and sustaining a welcoming and inclusive educational environment for students and maintaining its commitment to social justice.   The University is one of the most diverse private liberal arts institutions in the state of Michigan and actively seeks inclusion in its students, faculty, and staff. The undergraduate student body is a mix of urban and rural students from a range of socioeconomic backgrounds, many of whom are first-generation university attendees. The University’s faculty and staff are committed to providing personalized, individualized attention for students who commit themselves to seeking academic and personal success.   Job Summary Provides exceptional customer service to students, staff, faculty and administration of The University of Olivet. This position is responsible for greeting visitors to Student Services, answering general questions, directing constituents to the appropriate person, performing general duties as it relates to student accounts, collections, work study and registration. Answers phones, maintains office staff calendars, assists the Student Account Specialist as needed.   Responsibilities Greets visitors to student services Directs/Assists constituents to proper personnel within Student Services, i.e. Financial Aid, Registrar Manages the student ID card process and order supplies as needed Assists with student billing/collection through phone calls, emails, etc. Receives and applies payments to student accounts Receives and applies cash receipts from departments Distributes work study, refund, and reimbursement checks, as well as approved petty cash requests to students, staff and faculty Maintains cash drawer and receipts Answers all incoming phone calls Maintains and orders supplies for the office Maintains a professional and welcoming office space and environment Coordinates the bulletin boards inside and outside Student Services Sorts and delivers incoming departmental mail Manages mail that has been returned undeliverable Provides exceptional customer service experiences for every visitor Other duties as assigned   Accountabilities Direct/Assist students regarding financial aid, student account, registrar and works study questions Accurately maintain the cash drawer Provide assistance to the student account specialist, including billing, collections and payment plans Provide exceptional customer service experience for all visitors to Student Services Manage phone system for the office Manage schedules and appointments for student Services staff Maintain a professional and welcoming environment in the Student Services center Perform duties in a diverse, challenging and occasionally stressful environment Education and Experience   Required:  Associate degree or equivalent experience and a minimum of one (1) year experience in an office at an administrative assistant level are required for this position   Preferred:  Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience and 3 years’ experience in an office setting as an administrative assistant Working Conditions:  Work is normally performed in an office environment. Hazards:  Mainly those present in a normal office setting; no known hazards.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1e5bff11-ae4c-4b3c-a51f-a1212f1c4119&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201583836531_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Simulation and Lab Coordinator (9 month position)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Olivet\n\nThe University of Olivet was founded in 1844 as an institution of higher education open to all regardless of race, gender, or ability to pay. The University’s faculty and staff continue its tradition of creating and sustaining a welcoming and inclusive educational environment for students and maintaining its commitment to social justice.  The University is one of the most diverse private liberal arts institutions in the state of Michigan and actively seeks diversity in its students, faculty, and staff. The undergraduate student body is a mix of urban and rural students from a range of socioeconomic backgrounds, many of whom are first-generation university attendees. The University’s faculty and staff are committed to providing personalized, individualized attention for students who commit themselves to seeking academic and personal success.  The University of Olivet is seeking a Simulation Lab Clinical Coordinator to support the Nursing Program and join their growing team!  Position Summary The University of Olivet Nursing Program seeks a full-time Simulation and Lab Coordinator to operate the nursing skills and simulation laboratories and to coordinate clinical placements for the Pre-Licensure BSN program. The program admits a new cohort each semester, with multiple cohorts running concurrent skills lab, simulation, and clinical rotations at any given time. This position is central to delivering that instruction: the coordinator prepares and runs simulation scenarios, maintains the lab and its equipment, and secures and manages clinical placements across partner facilities. This is a 9-month position, July 1 through April 30. A nursing degree or clinical license is not required. This is an operational and technical role. The coordinator works alongside nursing faculty, who retain responsibility for instruction, clinical content, and student evaluation. We welcome applicants from simulation operations, allied health, emergency medical services, instructional technology, audiovisual production, healthcare administration, and similar backgrounds. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Simulation and Skills Lab Operations Set up, program, operate, and tear down high- and low-fidelity manikins for simulation sessions; troubleshoot equipment and coordinate manufacturer service and warranty repairs. Build out simulation scenarios in the manikin software from clinical content provided by faculty, including physiologic states, scenario branching, moulage, props, medications, and environmental setup. Operate the simulation audiovisual and recording system, including camera control, session capture, annotation, and retrieval of recordings for debriefing and faculty review. Serve as simulation operator during live sessions, running the manikin and adjusting scenario parameters at faculty direction; voice the patient when the scenario calls for it. Prepare, stock, and reset skills lab stations for skills training and competency testing days; support faculty during testing with setup, materials, timing, and station logistics. Maintain lab inventory and supply ordering; track budgets, par levels, expiration dates, and equipment maintenance schedules. Maintain lab safety, infection control, and sharps and hazardous materials protocols. Manage lab scheduling and access, including open lab hours and student practice time. Clinical Coordination Assistant Track and verify student clinical compliance requirements, including immunization records, background checks, drug screening, physicals, CPR certification, and facility-specific onboarding requirements. Maintain accurate placement and compliance records for program and accreditation reporting. Program Support Maintain documentation of simulation activities, clinical hours, and lab utilization to support CCNE accreditation reporting. Support faculty in applying INACSL Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best Practice to scenario setup, prebriefing logistics, and debriefing environments. Support program events including open houses, skills days, and orientation. Other duties as assigned in support of the nursing program. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a related field. Related fields include health sciences, allied health, emergency medical services, healthcare administration, education, instructional technology, information technology, media or audiovisual production, biology, or a comparable discipline. Two or more years of experience in a healthcare, simulation, laboratory, education, or technical operations setting. Demonstrated aptitude with technical equipment, software configuration, and hands-on troubleshooting. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple concurrent schedules, deadlines, and compliance records with accuracy. Ability to work effectively with faculty, students, and external facility partners, and to maintain confidentiality of student records under FERPA. Ability to lift and move equipment and manikins (up to [50] lbs) and to stand for extended periods during lab sessions. Preferred Qualifications Experience operating healthcare simulation manikins and simulation management or AV capture software. Certified Healthcare Simulation Operations Specialist (CHSOS), or willingness to pursue certification with institutional support. A current or prior healthcare credential such as paramedic, EMT, respiratory therapist, surgical technologist, medical assistant, LPN, or CNA. Prior experience in higher education, a hospital education department, or clinical placement coordination. Audiovisual, IT support, or media production experience. Familiarity with CCNE accreditation, the AACN Essentials, and clinical compliance tracking systems. Compensation and Benefits The anticipated hiring range for this position is $50,000 to $58,000 annually, depending on qualifications and directly relevant experience. The University of Olivet offers health, dental, and vision coverage; retirement contribution; paid time off; tuition benefits. The University supports professional development, including pursuit of CHSOS certification. To Apply Submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. The University of Olivet is an equal opportunity employer.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1e5bff11-ae4c-4b3c-a51f-a1212f1c4119&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201583835315_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing (9-month position)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Olivet\n\nPosition Summary The University of Olivet Nursing Program seeks a full-time nursing faculty member to teach across the Pre-Licensure BSN curriculum. The program admits a new cohort each semester and uses an integrated course model: each semester, a cohort takes one combined course carrying up to eight credit hours and containing didactic instruction, skills lab, simulation, and clinical rotation components. Faculty in this program therefore teach across all four settings rather than in a single modality and follow a cohort through a full semester of learning. This is a 9-month position, July 1 - April 30. This is a teaching-centered position at a small institution where faculty have direct influence over curriculum, course design, and program growth. The successful candidate will join a program actively building its course portfolio and preparing for CCNE accreditation review, with meaningful opportunity to shape both. Possible Teaching Responsibilities Didactic •      Teach assigned nursing courses using a flipped classroom model in which students complete reading and preparation before class. •      Anticipated content needs include mental health nursing, pathopharmacology, nursing fundamentals, comprehensive nursing care, and family centered care. final assignment will be based on candidate background and program need. •      Maintain course content in Canvas, including weekly modules, quizzes, midterm and final examinations. •      Integrate program resources including Kaplan NCLEX preparation materials and the program curriculum map. Skills Lab and Simulation •      Teach and supervise skills training days, including demonstration, supervised practice, and competency validation. •      Facilitate simulation sessions, including prebriefing, scenario facilitation, and structured debriefing consistent with INACSL Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best Practice. •      Provide clinical scenario content and learning objectives to the Simulation and Lab Coordinator, who handles scenario build, manikin operation, and lab setup. •      Evaluate student performance in lab and simulation against course competencies. Clinical •      Supervise student clinical rotations at partner facilities, maintaining ratios consistent with facility agreements and Michigan Board of Nursing requirements. •      Evaluate clinical performance, complete clinical evaluations, and provide ongoing feedback and remediation. •      Maintain professional relationships with unit staff and facility educators at assigned sites. •      Complete facility-specific onboarding and maintain current compliance requirements (immunizations, background check, CPR, facility orientation). Additional Responsibilities •      Advise and mentor nursing students, including academic advising and NCLEX preparation support. •      Participate in program assessment, curriculum review, and CCNE accreditation activities, including documentation of student learning outcomes. •      Contribute to admissions, recruitment, orientation, and program events. •      Serve on department and university committees. •      Maintain a program of scholarship appropriate to rank and consistent with the institution's expectations for teaching, discovery, integration, and application. •      Participate in professional development to maintain currency in clinical practice and nursing education. Required Qualifications •      Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited program. •      Current, unencumbered license to practice as a Registered Nurse in the State of Michigan, or eligibility for licensure by the start date. •      Minimum of two years of direct clinical nursing practice. •      Demonstrated ability to teach or precept in clinical, lab, or classroom settings. •      Ability to meet clinical facility health and compliance requirements. Preferred Qualifications •      Prior full-time or adjunct teaching experience in a pre-licensure nursing program. •      Clinical background in mental health, medical-surgical, or family centered care. •      Experience with simulation facilitation and debriefing. •      Experience with Canvas or a comparable learning management system. To Apply Submit a cover letter addressing teaching philosophy and clinical background, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references.  The University of Olivet is an equal opportunity employer.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
